            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %h2#references References
          %p A condensed write-up of the mathematics needed for stating the above formal definition of manifold-diagrammatic higher categories was compiled in
          %ul
            %li#Zero23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Dorn"}> Christoph Dorn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em From zero to manifold-diagrammatric categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://cxdorn.github.io/assets/pdfs/zero-to-mdhc.pdf"} pdf
          %p and explained in
          %ul
            %li
              From zero to manifold diagrams, TallCat Seminar Talk, (
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=67RAzY-13r4"}> video
              )
          %p A general introduction to some of the relevant ideas in the area can be found in
          %ul
            %li#NCC
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2023/03/an_invitation_to_geometric_hig.html"}> An Invitation to Geometric Higher Categories
              ,
              = succeed "-Category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p with further details spelled out in
          %ul
            %li#Dorn23
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Dorn"}> Christoph Dorn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Nine short stories about geometric higher categories
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://cxdorn.github.io/assets/pdfs/nine-stories.pdf"} pdf
          %p The type of ‘directed combinatorial topology’ that governs the stratified topology of manifold diagrams was described in
          %ul
            %li#DornDouglas21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Dorn"} Christoph Dorn
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Douglas"} Christopher Douglas
              = succeed "," do
